{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788308669,"nonce":"O8HJvOX4nrjioNWCGfgscUnglDY=","message":"AMENDMENT to comment #8 — Evan's rulings of 2026-09-01, filed before the run's first advance.\n\nTwo clauses of #8's \"Fixture and staging\" and one of its \"Fixture\" line are superseded. Recorded here rather than left in a transcript, because #8 is the contract the run is graded against.\n\n\n\nCrashlanded gives 3 colonists, ~50 survival meals, 30 medicine, 30 components, 800 silver, three weapons and a flak set — all forbidden where the pods dropped it. It gives no wood and no steel. Getting them is the run:\n\n- wood is trees — `designate {type:\"chop\"}`; colonists never fell on their own initiative ([[materials-are-a-standing-loop]]);\n- steel is compacted steel in rock (`designate {type:\"mine\"}`), loose steel on the map, or a trader against the 800 silver.\n\nA steel shortage is therefore **not a blocker to escalate**. Solving it is the graded work.\n\nConsequences for the tables:\n\n- **G2's staging watermark is seq 0** unless `dev:set-skill` is used (below). There is no staging phase.\n- **T4 / T5 / T6 lose the clause \"the base room does not count.\"** Nothing was given, so every room on the map is colonist-built by construction and there is nothing to trace. Each graded room is still identified by an interior cell and read at day 20, since room ids do not survive construction (`d16a463`).\n- Day 1 is a real RimWorld opening: forbidden gear, no walls, Spring, night coming. Shelter and a heat source before anyone sleeps outdoors is a G1 problem, not a flavour one.\n\n\n`build` and `place-layout --mode blueprint` (the default) are the only placement routes for the whole run.\n\n`--mode instant` journals as an `action` row, **not** a `dev` row, so G2 cannot catch it. That makes instant mode a discipline obligation rather than an enforced one, and the run report states explicitly that it was not used.\n\nThe one sanctioned exception is **`dev:set-skill`, and only where `work-cover` reports `still_under`** — i.e. the roster genuinely cannot meet a floor the mod itself defines (Doctor at 2 is the usual one, [[one-doctor-is-zero-doctors]]). Every use is listed in the report with the `still_under` row that justified it. If it is never needed there are zero `dev` rows in the run and G2's watermark is seq 0.\n\n\n\n\nEverything else in #8 stands as written: the twenty-day goal, G1/G3/G4/G5, T1/T2/T3/T7, the storyteller untouched with no `dev:incident` fallback, the procedure (`playbook/PLAY-LOOP.md` in `SESSION-START.md` order), the out-of-scope list, the deliverables list, and Dorian's sign-off as the hard gate.\n\nThe run directory is `RUNS/m1-20260901/`; `RWA_RUN=m1-20260901`.","files":null}]}